  "notes": "{喫煙|きつえん} is the formal term for smoking, commonly used in public signage and official contexts.\n\nKANJI BREAKDOWN:\n- {喫|きつ} (to consume, to drink/smoke)\n- {煙|えん} (smoke)\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {喫煙|きつえん}{所|じょ}/{喫煙|きつえん}{室|しつ} (smoking area/room)\n- {喫煙|きつえん}{者|しゃ} (smoker)\n- {喫煙|きつえん}{席|せき} (smoking seats)\n- {喫煙|きつえん}{習慣|しゅうかん} (smoking habit)\n- {受動|じゅどう}{喫煙|きつえん} (passive smoking, secondhand smoke)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {喫煙|きつえん}する (to smoke - suru verb)\n- {喫煙|きつえん}{可|か} (smoking allowed)\n- {喫煙|きつえん}{不可|ふか} (no smoking)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nJapan has increasingly restricted smoking in public spaces. Many train stations, restaurants, and public buildings now have designated {喫煙|きつえん}{所|じょ} (smoking areas) or are entirely {禁煙|きんえん} (non-smoking).",
